===Withdrawn bids===
* Vlaho Orepić withdrew on 2 December. He had initially scheduled the submission of his signatures of endorsement to the State Electoral Commission for 3 December 2019, however after having managed to collect only 8,054 signatures by the evening of 2 December, he determined that he would be unlikely to reach the required quota of 10,000 signatures by the set deadline and he thus withdrew his candidacy.<ref>{{cite web |title=VLAHO OREPIĆ ODUSTAO OD KANDIDATURE ZA PREDSJEDNIKA Skupio premalo potpisa, kaže da je građane bilo strah podržati ga: 'Govorili su mi da ne smiju' |url=https://www.jutarnji.hr/vijesti/hrvatska/vlaho-orepic-odustao-od-kandidature-za-predsjednika-skupio-premalo-potpisa-kaze-da-je-gradane-bilo-strah-podrzati-ga-govorili-su-mi-da-ne-smiju/9694564/ |website=jutarnji.hr |date=2 December 2019 |access-date=3 December 2019}}</ref> He is a member of the [[Croatian Parliament]] (2017–) and the former [[Ministry of the Interior (Croatia)|Minister of the Interior]] (2016–2017). He had announced his bid on 11 July.
* Tomislav Panenić withdrew on 3 December.<ref name="direktno-odustali">{{cite web |title=HOĆE LI STIĆI? Pernar se pohvalio uspjehom, Radnička fronta još šuti |url=https://direktno.hr/domovina/hoce-li-stici-pernar-se-pohvalio-uspjehom-radnicka-fronta-jos-suti-174905/ |website=direktno.hr |date=3 December 2019 |access-date=3 December 2019 |language=hr |archive-date=3 December 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191203123629/https://direktno.hr/domovina/hoce-li-stici-pernar-se-pohvalio-uspjehom-radnicka-fronta-jos-suti-174905/ |url-status=dead }}</ref> He is a current member of the [[Croatian Parliament]] (2016–) and the former [[Ministry of Economy, Entrepreneurship and Crafts (Croatia)|Minister of Economy]] (2016). His had announced his bid on 26 June.
* Ante Simonić withdrew on 3 December.<ref name="direktno-odustali"/> He is a former [[Deputy Prime Minister of Croatia]], having served in the [[Cabinet of Ivica Račan II|Second Račan cabinet]]. He had announced his bid on 14 July.

=== Failed candidacies ===
These individuals failed to submit the required number of endorsement signatures.
*Slobodan Midžić, a perennial potential candidate who submitted just one signature of endorsement to the State Electoral Commission on 3 December 2019.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.index.hr/vijesti/clanak/u-dip-dosao-covjek-koji-sebe-naziva-kraljem-hrvata-iz-sjene-predao-jedan-potpis/2137569.aspx|title = U DIP došao čovjek koji sebe naziva kraljem Hrvata iz sjene, predao jedan potpis}}</ref> He had previously unsuccessfully attempted to become an official candidate in the [[2009–10 Croatian presidential election|2009]] and the [[2014–15 Croatian presidential election|2014]] elections.
* Josip Juretić, an activist. His bid was announced on 7 September.<ref>{{cite web |title=Kandidata nikad dosta: u predsjedničku utrku uključio se Josip Juretić, čovjek koji protiv Hrvatske vodi 105 parnica, a nedavno je na Markov trg donio lijes |url=https://www.slobodnadalmacija.hr/novosti/hrvatska/clanak/id/622154/kandidata-nikad-dosta-u-predsjednicku-utrku-ukljucio-se-josip-juretic-covjek-koji-protiv-hrvatske-vodi-105-parnica-a-nedavno-je-na-markov-trg-donio-lijes |website=slobodnadalmacija.hr |date=7 September 2019 |access-date=3 December 2019}}</ref>
* Ivan Rude, a lawyer from [[Šibenik]]. His bid was announced on 16 September.<ref>{{cite web |title=Šibenski odvjetnik Ivan Rude objavio kandidaturu za predsjednika RH: 'Ovo je igra na sve ili ništa' |url=https://www.sibenik.in/sibenik/sibenski-odvjetnik-ivan-rude-objavio-kandidaturu-za-predsjednika-rh-ovo-je-igra-na-sve-ili-nista/112397.html |website=sibenik.in |access-date=3 December 2019}}</ref>
* Ava Karabatić, a TV personality, singer, and model from [[Zadar]]. Her bid was announced on 30 September. Subsequently, she endorsed Zoran Milanović.{{citation needed|date=December 2019}}
* David Lucijan Rožman, a student. His bid was announced on 1 October.
* Antun Babić, a former [[deputy chief of mission]]-minister plenipotentiary in the Croatian embassy in [[Ireland]].<ref name="Babic">{{cite web |url=https://direktno.hr/direkt/analizirali-smo-predstojeci-predsjednicki-izbori-mogli-bi-po-broju-kandidata-premasiti-i-one-2005-godine-163737/ |title=Analizirali smo: Predstojeći predsjednički izbori mogli bi po broju kandidata premašiti i one 2005 godine |date=7 August 2019 |access-date=29 August 2019 |publisher=[[Direktno.hr]] |language=hr |trans-title= We have analyzed: The upcoming presidential elections could have even more candidates then those in 2005}}</ref> His bid was announced on 14 February 2019<ref name="Babic-declared">{{cite web |url=http://pozeskivodic.com/pleternicanin-antun-babic-bivsi-emigrant-u-australiji-savjetnik-predsjednika-tudmana-i-diplomat-pred-banskim-dvorima-najavio-kandidaturu-za-predsjednika-rh/ |title=Pleterničanin Antun Babić Bivši emigrant u Australiji, savjetnik Predsjednika Tuđmana i diplomat pred Banskim dvorima najavio kandidaturu za Predsjednika RH! |date=15 February 2019 |access-date=29 August 2019 |publisher=[[Požeški vodič]] |language=hr |archive-date=29 August 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190829145837/http://pozeskivodic.com/pleternicanin-antun-babic-bivsi-emigrant-u-australiji-savjetnik-predsjednika-tudmana-i-diplomat-pred-banskim-dvorima-najavio-kandidaturu-za-predsjednika-rh/ |url-status=dead }}</ref>
* Goran Jurišić, a member of [[HSP 1861]]. His bid was announced on 3 January 2019.<ref name="Jurisic-declared">{{Cite web|url=https://hrvatski-pravaski-dom.webnode.hr/l/obracanje-stovateljima-lika-i-djela-predsjednika-tudmana/|title=Obraćanje štovateljima lika i djela Predsjednika Tuđmana|date=2019-01-19|website=hrvatski-pravaski-dom.webnode.hr|access-date=2019-11-13|quote=profesor Goran Jurišić iz Zagreba nestranački kandidat za predsjednika Republike Hrvatske, te je to ujedno i prva kandidatura, i prva objavljena kandidatura u Hrvatskoj, prije bilo koga drugog, što je VIJEST, te Vam je stavljamo na raspolaganje, uključujući link na YouTube-kanal JurišićaZaPredsjednika, gdje je ista objavljena 3. siječnja 2019. godine. }}</ref>
