==== Debates ====
After official validation of candidates by the State Electoral Commission, the first debate was a confrontation between [[Katarina Peović]] ([[Workers' Front (Croatia)|RF]] and [[Socialist Labour Party of Croatia|SRP]]) and [[Anto Đapić]] (''Democratic Alliance for National Renewal''), the most left-wing and the most-right wing candidate respectively, which was filmed by and broadcast on [[N1 (TV channel)|N1]] television on 5 December 2019.<ref name="Peovic-vs-Dapic">{{cite web |title=Prvo sučeljavanje u Pressingu: Peović vs Đapić |url=http://hr.n1info.com/Vijesti/a465509/Prvo-suceljavanje-u-Pressingu-Peovic-vs-Djapic.html |language=hr |publisher=[[N1 (TV channel)|N1]] |date=5 December 2019 |access-date=5 December 2019 |archive-date=5 December 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191205205512/http://hr.n1info.com/Vijesti/a465509/Prvo-suceljavanje-u-Pressingu-Peovic-vs-Djapic.html |url-status=dead }}</ref>

On 17 December, the [[Croatian Radiotelevision]] held the general debate with all 11 candidates participated.<ref>{{cite web |title=PREDSJEDNIČKI IZBORI Veliko sučeljavanja kandidata na HRT-u, pratite uživo |url=http://novilist.hr/Vijesti/Hrvatska/PREDSJEDNICKI-IZBORI-Veliko-suceljavanja-kandidata-na-HRT-u-pratite-uzivo |website=novilist.hr |access-date=18 December 2019 |archive-date=18 December 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191218085558/http://novilist.hr/Vijesti/Hrvatska/PREDSJEDNICKI-IZBORI-Veliko-suceljavanja-kandidata-na-HRT-u-pratite-uzivo |url-status=dead }}</ref> It was the only debate where all first-round candidates participated.

